{"id": "mm6405a1", "status": "ok", "message_id": "msg_011CggGVWK8tZWYMu7pxqzyo", "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "errors": [], "usage": {"input": 9183, "output": 3357}, "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "{\"id\": \"mm6405a1\", \"data_focus\": {\"v\": \"yes\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"The overall age-adjusted silicosis death rate for blacks (0.87 per 1 million) was significantly higher than the rate for whites (0.59).\"}]}, \"outcome_types\": [{\"v\": \"count/rate\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"The annual number of silicosis deaths declined from 164 (0.74 per 1 million) in 2001 to 101 (0.39) in 2010\"}]}], \"analytic_depth\": [{\"v\": \"summary\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"table 1\", \"q\": \"\\\"1,437\\\",0.59,(0.56–0.62)\"}]}, {\"v\": \"comparison\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"The age-adjusted silicosis death rate for males (1.39 per 1 million) was significantly higher than the rate for females.\"}]}, {\"v\": \"stratified/adjusted\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"Death rates were age-adjusted to the 2000 standard U.S. population.\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Trends in annual age-adjusted death rates per 1 million population were examined using a first-order autoregressive linear regression model.\"}]}], \"study_design\": [{\"v\": \"surveillance/descriptive\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"CDC analyzed annual multiple cause-of-death data for 2001–2010 for decedents aged ≥15 years.\"}]}, {\"v\": \"before/after or trend\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"A statistically significant decline in silicosis death rates was observed during 2001–2010.\"}]}], \"methods_quotes\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Trends in annual age-adjusted death rates per 1 million population were examined using a first-order autoregressive linear regression model.\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Differences in death rates were considered to be statistically significant if 9